          "chunk_id": "s03_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c4_existing_approaches_like_adaptive_re",
          "text": "Existing approaches like Adaptive Retrieval simply learn when to skip the search, but when they skip they fall back entirely on the base language model and discard the retrieval distribution, which hurts most in domains where the base model is weak.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
